{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-39422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,i+(x+y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path  $r(t)=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t\\,i+2j$ for $t\\in [0,\\frac{1}{2}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-39422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t,\\,y=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t+2)\\,j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t+2)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(2t\\,i+(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡t+2)\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,i) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}\\,dt \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =-2(\\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-39422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c22bbaf962e90b9111fd5adfdc9e0dd60b47729054c76f196532e7ec3a7a5c67"} {"question" "q-39422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-39422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2+\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "-4-\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "1-\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "2-\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-39422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=(x+z)\\,i+(z-y)\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j+2t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y=3{t}^{2},\\,z=2t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(2t-3{t}^{2})\\,j+(2t)^{2}\\,k \\\\  & =(2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(2t-3{t}^{2})\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)j \\\\  & =2ti+6t\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =((2t+{t}^{2})\\,i+(2t-3{t}^{2})\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (2ti+6t\\,j+2\\,k) \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}+12{t}^{2}-18{t}^{3}+8{t}^{2} \\\\  & =24{t}^{2}-16{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(24{t}^{2}-16{t}^{3})\\,dt \\\\  & ={8{t}^{3}-4{t}^{4}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =8-4 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c22bbaf962e90b9111fd5adfdc9e0dd60b47729054c76f196532e7ec3a7a5c67"} {"question" "q-124669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124669" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate  ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=x\\,i+y\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i+y\\,j \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot ((\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j) \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =t{sin}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t{cos}^{2}⁡t-{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =t({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }t\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{2}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =2{\\pi }^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c22bbaf962e90b9111fd5adfdc9e0dd60b47729054c76f196532e7ec3a7a5c67"} {"question" "q-124691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "2{\\pi }^{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "] ["math" "{\\pi }^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124691" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{\\pi }^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=\\frac{y+1}{x}\\,i-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+(t-1)\\,j$ for $t\\in [3,4].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx={t}^{2},\\,y=t-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{y+1}{x}\\,i-\\frac{2(x-1)}{y}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{(t-1)+1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i-\\frac{2({t}^{2}-1)}{t-1}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-2(t+1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)j \\\\  & =2t\\,i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{t}\\,i-2(t+1)\\,j)\\cdot (2t\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot 2t-2(t+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-2(t+1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(-2t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={[-{t}^{2}]}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[-16+9] \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124696" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c22bbaf962e90b9111fd5adfdc9e0dd60b47729054c76f196532e7ec3a7a5c67"} {"question" "q-124696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-11"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-124696" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-165421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{x}\\,i+\\sqrt{y}\\,j+z\\,k$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=t\\,i+t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ for $t\\in [1,2].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-165421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have \n\n$$\nx=t,\\,y=t,\\,z={t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\sqrt{x}\\,i+\\sqrt{y}\\,j+z\\,k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+\\sqrt{t}\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+j+2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\sqrt{t}\\,i+\\sqrt{t}\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k)\\cdot (i+j+2t\\,k) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t}+\\sqrt{t}+2{t}^{3} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{t}+2{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F(r)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(2\\sqrt{t}+2{t}^{3})\\,dt \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3/2}+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}+8-\\frac{4}{3}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16\\sqrt{2}+37}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-165421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c22bbaf962e90b9111fd5adfdc9e0dd60b47729054c76f196532e7ec3a7a5c67"} {"question" "q-165421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-165421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{10\\sqrt{2}+45}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{16\\sqrt{2}+37}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}+31}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}+32}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}+47}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0029fb16fdc32f29bee5cb6ada122c3195e4141f44316e15106938c14edd0f"} {"question" "q-165421" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16\\sqrt{2}+37}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e